ineering handshake.</description><pubDate>Thu, 23 Apr 2026 13:03:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>The Technology System</title><link>https://www.novifyx.com/posts/ems-the-technology-system/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.novifyx.com/posts/ems-the-technology-system/</guid><description>Tech debt as a system outcome. Quality as a loop. Architecture as a ripple.</description><pubDate>Thu, 23 Apr 2026 13:02:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>The People System</title><link>https://www.novifyx.com/posts/ems-the-people-system/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.novifyx.com/posts/ems-the-people-system/</guid><description>Hiring, onboarding, growth and retention as one connected loop.</description><pubDate>Thu, 23 Apr 2026 13:01:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Why Systems, Not Processes</title><link>https://www.novifyx.com/posts/ems-why-systems-not-processes/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.novifyx.com/posts/ems-why-systems-not-processes/</guid><description>Why engineering management is a systems problem, not a process problem. The opening article of a seven-part series.</description><pubDate>Thu, 23 Apr 2026 13:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>What It Really Means to Be a Senior Software Engineer</title><link>https://www.novifyx.com/posts/what-it-really-means-to-be-a-senior-software-engineer/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.novifyx.com/posts/what-it-really-means-to-be-a-senior-software-engineer/</guid><description>Your commit history doesn&apos;t make you a senior engineer. True seniors provide solutions that balance time, resources and maintenance. They organize the work and communicate with stakeholders.</description><pubDate>Sat, 28 Feb 2026 16:54:16 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>The Scaling Handbook</title><link>https://www.novifyx.com/posts/the-scaling-handbook/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.novifyx.com/posts/the-scaling-handbook/</guid><description>Practical frameworks for leading engineering teams through chaos, scaling and high-growth environments inspired by Molly Graham&apos;s insights.</description><pubDate>Mon, 12 Jan 2026 19:28:06 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Two Horses asses standard, is it that bad?</title><link>https://www.novifyx.com/posts/two-horses-asses-is-it-that-bad/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.novifyx.com/posts/two-horses-asses-is-it-that-bad/</guid><description>An attempt to debunk the &quot;two horses&apos; asses&quot; myth to reveal how standards truly drive innovation and a confrontation of the corporate fiction of a &quot;High Care, High Performance&quot; culture by arguing that leaders must make a conscious trade-off between the two.</description><pubDate>Fri, 31 Oct 2025 00:13:30 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Motivation is a trap. Build a system instead.</title><link>https://www.novifyx.com/tips/motivation-is-a-trap/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.novifyx.com/tips/motivation-is-a-trap/</guid><description>Motivation is a trap. Build a system instead.</description><pubDate>Sat, 18 Oct 2025 15:34:38 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Prioritize systems over solo effort</title><link>https://www.novifyx.com/tips/systems-and-teams/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.novifyx.com/tips/systems-and-teams/</guid><description>Prioritize systems over solo effort</description><pubDate>Tue, 14 Oct 2025 18:15:38 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>How We Engineered Our Leadership Team&apos;s Purpose</title><link>https://www.novifyx.com/posts/from-skeptic-to-champion/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.novifyx.com/posts/from-skeptic-to-champion/</guid><description>This is the story of how a structured process, focused on defining our team&apos;s &quot;Why, How and What&quot;, transformed my perspective and engineered a new sense of clarity, alignment and shared purpose for our entire leadership team</description><pubDate>Sun, 28 Sep 2025 16:53:52 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Dad-Ops Playbook</title><link>https://www.novifyx.com/posts/dad-ops-playbook/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.novifyx.com/posts/dad-ops-playbook/</guid><description>Facing engineering burnout and scaling challenges? This article introduces &quot;Dad-Ops&quot; - a leadership playbook that applies five core fatherhood principles to build more resilient, creative and high-performing teams</description><pubDate>Mon, 01 Sep 2025 23:23:38 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Speed vs Process</title><link>https://www.novifyx.com/posts/speed-vs-process/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.novifyx.com/posts/speed-vs-process/</guid><description>Urgency beats purity, communication keeps the team with you. Faced with an urgent integration and scarce capacity, we chose the least-damaging path. Simple learning is - decisions win the moment but communication sustains the team.</description><pubDate>Sat, 23 Aug 2025 17:19:41 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Your Team Is Only as Fast as Its Slowest Engineer</title><link>https://www.novifyx.com/posts/your-team-is-only-as-fast-as-its-slowest-engineer/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.novifyx.com/posts/your-team-is-only-as-fast-as-its-slowest-engineer/</guid><description>Can you care deeply about your team and still fire someone? &quot;A-players hire A-players, B-players hire C-players&quot;, we&apos;ve all heard it - but reality is messy. My story about building an &quot;A-team&quot; without becoming ruthless - and why sometimes the kindest thing a leader can do is also the hardest thing.</description><pubDate>Fri, 15 Aug 2025 01:53:01 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>What the heck is EOS?</title><link>https://www.novifyx.com/posts/what-the-heck-is-eos/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.novifyx.com/posts/what-the-heck-is-eos/</guid><description>A review of &quot;What the Heck is EOS?&quot;, exploring its potential to improve collaboration and structure while addressing its limitations, repetitive writing, and reliance on people fo